---
/**
 * Privacy policy for the Tether Health app (WEB-014, draft).
 *
 * The app privacy policy URL Google Play and the App Store ask for. Content
 * describes the app as documented in the Tether-Health repository when this
 * draft was written. No source path or evidence note ships in the HTML.
 *
 * Anything the sources do not state is a visible "To be confirmed" line.
 * Nothing here is final legal text: it needs counsel and the owner.
 *
 * Not built: the leading underscore in the file name makes Astro skip it,
 * so /app-privacy/ does not exist in the build, the sitemap or any link. It
 * stays that way until it is rewritten for the final app and counsel signs
 * off. Publishing then means renaming the file, removing noindex and the
 * draft notice, linking it, and updating test/functional/app-privacy.test.js
 * in the same change. This page does not replace privacy.astro, which covers
 * the website only.
 */

import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import SupportEmail from "../components/SupportEmail.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const appName = "Tether Health";
const packageName = "com.TetherHealthLLC.tetherhealth";
---

<Base
  title={`${appName} app privacy policy`}
  description={`How the ${appName} app collects, uses and keeps your information, who handles it for us, and how to delete it or contact us.`}
  noindex
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title={`${appName} app privacy policy`}
    intro={`How the ${appName} app, developed by ${site.legalName}, handles your information.`}
    width="narrow"
  />

  <Section width="narrow">
    <p
      class="mb-12 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-3xl border border-mint-strong bg-mint p-6 leading-relaxed text-teal-mid"
    >
      <Icon name="info" size={20} class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-teal-deep" />
      <span>
        Draft for review by {site.legalName} and its counsel. Items marked "To be
        confirmed" are not decided yet.
      </span>
    </p>

    <div class="prose-tether">
      <h2>About this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers the {appName} app (Android package {packageName}),
        developed by {site.legalName}.
      </p>
      <p>
        It does not cover www.tetherhealthgroup.com, which has its own privacy
        notice.
      </p>
      <p>To be confirmed: the date this policy takes effect.</p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: whether this policy also covers an iOS version of the
        app.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the app as a guest</h2>
      <p>
        You can use the app as a guest, without an account. While you use the
        app as a guest, your data is kept on your device only.
      </p>
      <p>
        As a guest, your quit plan and any Heartwise, Steady or ClearAir entries
        are stored on your device.
      </p>
      <p>
        Heartwise, Steady or ClearAir entries you make as a guest are not
        uploaded to an account when you later sign in.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you sign in on a phone that holds a guest quit plan, the app asks
        whether to back it up to your account. It uploads the plan only if you
        agree.
      </p>
      <p>
        The daily check-in, Craving Rescue, the stress reset, slip recovery and
        medication status are held only while the app is open. They are not
        saved and not sent.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect when you have an account</h2>
      <p>If you create an account and sign in, the app collects:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your email address</li>
        <li>an account ID that links your data to your account</li>
        <li>a display name, if you set one</li>
        <li>a profile photo, if you add one</li>
        <li>
          your quit plan: how much you smoke, your triggers, your readiness and
          quit path, your quit date, your reasons and preparation tasks, your
          treatment-support and care-team-reminder settings, and any
          support-person names, relationships and check-in text you type in
        </li>
        <li>
          program health data, if you use Heartwise, Steady or ClearAir: blood
          pressure readings, cholesterol panels, glucose-style readings, target
          ranges, your ClearAir clinician plan, symptom logs, peak flow, zone
          and notes
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Anything you type into a free-text field, such as a note or the name of
        a clinician, is saved with that entry.
      </p>
      <p>
        You choose a profile photo from your photo library. The app does not ask
        for camera access.
      </p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: how a profile photo is handled when it is uploaded.
      </p>
      <p>The app keeps a sign-in session on your device.</p>
      <p>
        The app does not ask for permission to use your location, contacts or
        microphone.
      </p>
      <p>The app has no ads and sends no analytics or crash reports.</p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: what our service providers record when the app connects
        to them, such as your IP address and the web addresses the app calls,
        and for how long.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <p>
        We use your information to run the app: to create your account and sign
        you in, to save your quit plan and program entries to your account, and
        to show you your own data.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use your email address to create your account, sign you in and reset
        your password.
      </p>
      <p>We do not sell your health data.</p>
      <p>
        We do not share your information with third parties for their own use.
      </p>
      <p>The app has no feature for sharing your data with other users.</p>

      <h2>Who handles your information for us</h2>
      <p>These service providers handle your information to run the app:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Supabase, for sign-in accounts, the database and photo storage. Our
          Supabase database is in the West US region.
        </li>
        <li>
          An application server that handles your profile, quit plan, program
          data, data copy and account deletion.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: which company hosts the production application server,
        and where it runs.
      </p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: which service sends the sign-up confirmation and
        password-reset emails.
      </p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: the contract terms we have with our service providers.
      </p>

      <h2>Protection in transit</h2>
      <p>
        A release build of the app refuses to connect to a service address that
        does not use HTTPS.
      </p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: how your data is protected on your phone, in transit
        and at our service providers.
      </p>

      <h2>Keeping and deleting your information</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your account and data in the app. The steps, and what to
        do if you cannot sign in, are on the <a href="/delete-account/"
          >account deletion page</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: how long we keep your account data if you never delete
        your account.
      </p>
      <p>
        Copies of your data in backups and logs may remain after you delete your
        account.
      </p>
      <p>To be confirmed: how long backups and logs are kept.</p>
      <p>
        To remove your account's data from your device, delete the account,
        uninstall the app or clear its storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        Signed-in users can view their account data and copy it as text. The
        copy contains your profile, quit plan and program health data.
      </p>
      <p>
        A copy you make is outside the app and is not deleted when you delete
        your account.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        In the app you can view and copy your account data, change your display
        name and photo, and delete your account.
      </p>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to ask for
        access to, correction of or deletion of your personal data, to object to
        or restrict how we use it, and to complain to a data protection
        authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: which privacy laws apply to the app and which rights
        they give you.
      </p>
      <p>
        To use these rights, write to <SupportEmail mailbox="privacy" />.
      </p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: who answers these emails, how we check who you are, and
        how quickly we reply.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this policy, email <SupportEmail
          mailbox="privacy"
        />.
      </p>
      <p>
        For help with the app, email <SupportEmail />.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: the minimum age for the app (the draft recommendation
        is 18 and over), and what we do if we learn that a child has an account.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you believe a child has created an account, email <SupportEmail
          mailbox="privacy"
        />.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        When this policy changes, we will update the effective date on this
        page.
      </p>
      <p>
        To be confirmed: how people who already have an account will be told
        about a material change, for example inside the app.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
